From: NVX maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] tty: hvc: push the flip buffer under hp->lock

__hvc_poll() reads characters from the backend and inserts them into the
tty flip buffer under hp->lock, but pushes the flip buffer only after it
releases the lock. A backend that both interrupts and is polled by khvcd,
such as virtio-console, has two producers of the same flip buffer: the
hvc_poll() of its interrupt handler, and khvcd. The push commits the fill
of the tail buffer (tail->commit = tail->used). Pushed after the unlock,
one producer can commit a stale fill after the other one filled the same
tail further, committed it, and linked a new tail. flush_to_ldisc() then
takes the tail as read up to its stale commit and frees it, dropping the
characters past that commit: whole N_INBUF reads, up to a flip buffer of
input, lost without a trace. A reader that waits for a byte count, such as
a framed protocol on the tty, then waits forever.

Push the flip buffer before releasing hp->lock, which serializes the
producers. tty_flip_buffer_push() may be called in atomic context.

--- a/drivers/tty/hvc/hvc_console.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/hvc/hvc_console.c
@@ -745,15 +745,23 @@
 		tty_wakeup(tty);
 	}
  bail:
-	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hp->lock, flags);
-
 	if (read_total) {
 		/* Activity is occurring, so reset the polling backoff value to
 		   a minimum for performance. */
 		timeout = MIN_TIMEOUT;
 
+		/*
+		 * Push while hp->lock still serializes this poll with the other
+		 * producer of the flip buffer, the console's interrupt or khvcd.
+		 * The push commits the tail's fill. Pushed after the unlock, a
+		 * stale fill can be committed after the other producer filled the
+		 * tail further, committed it, and linked a new tail, and
+		 * flush_to_ldisc() then frees the tail without the characters
+		 * past the stale commit.
+		 */
 		tty_flip_buffer_push(&hp->port);
 	}
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hp->lock, flags);
 	tty_kref_put(tty);
 
 	return poll_mask;
